ll farmers markets minus the territories. First, let me see if there are any other territories in the data.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_016WVPqTFp2thtgghcty958H","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"farmers_markets","compose":"source.select('state_name')","limit":0}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":12,"output":243,"cacheRead":17577,"cacheWrite":501,"totalTokens":18333,"cost":{"input":0.000012,"output":0.0012150000000000002,"cacheRead":0.0017577,"cacheWrite":0.00062625,"total":0.0036109500000000004},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":118},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786913000660,"responseId":"msg_011Ce75VCNnFz5xdnbT366hv","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_016WVPqTFp2thtgghcty958H","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"state_name\"\n\"California\"\n\"New York\"\n\"Pennsylvania\"\n\"Minnesota\"\n\"Illinois\"\n\"Virginia\"\n\"Wisconsin\"\n\"Michigan\"\n\"Massachusetts\"\n\"Florida\"\n\"Georgia\"\n\"Ohio\"\n\"Texas\"\n\"Missouri\"\n\"North Carolina\"\n\"Iowa\"\n\"Kentucky\"\n\"Indiana\"\n\"Colorado\"\n\"Washington\"\n\"Maryland\"\n\"Connecticut\"\n\"Kansas\"\n\"Oregon\"\n\"Alabama\"\n\"Oklahoma\"\n\"Arizona\"\n\"Tennessee\"\n\"South Carolina\"\n\"New Jersey\"\n\"Montana\"\n\"Arkansas\"\n\"Louisiana\"\n\"Vermont\"\n\"Alaska\"\n\"Idaho\"\n\"West Virginia\"\n\"Wyoming\"\n\"Nebraska\"\n\"District Of Columbia\"\n\"New Hampshire\"\n\"Mississippi\"\n\"Delaware\"\n\"Maine\"\n\"New Mexico\"\n\"Rhode Island\"\n\"Utah\"\n\"Nevada\"\n\"North Dakota\"\n\"South Dakota\"\n\"Hawaii\"\n\"Puerto Rico\"\n\"Virgin Islands\"\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786913004927},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! So I can see the complete list. I see:\n- All 50 states\n- District of Columbia (which is not a state but is part of the U.S.)\n- Puerto Rico (territory)\n- Virgin Islands (territory)\n\nThe user asked for \"total farmers markets (excl. territories)\", so I should include all states and D.C., but exclude Puerto Rico and Virgin Islands. Let me now calculate the total.\n\nActually, I should create a derived metric that calculates this. According to the instructions, I should create a build script that reads both sources, joins them if needed, and derives the metric. However, in this case, I can do it with a single alias compose since the metric (total farmers markets per 100,000 residents) involves:\n1. Sum of farmers_markets from farmers_markets alias (excluding territories)\n2. The POPESTIMATE2025 value from the census_population alias (for United States)\n\nSince I need to join/combine data from both aliases, I should create a build script that reads both sources and creates the metric. But actually, I can do this with xorq_select by first computing each value separately and then combining them.\n\nLet me first get the total farmers markets excluding territories, then get the U.S. population, and then calculate the rate.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_013LfnzPmPbB4rdHVMZpDkV8","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"farmers_markets","compose":"source.filter(source.state_name != 'Puerto Rico').filter(source.state_name != 'Virgin Islands').aggregate(total_markets=source.farmers_markets.sum())","limit":1}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":13,"output":450,"cacheRead":18078,"cacheWrite":492,"totalTokens":19033,"cost":{"input":0.000013,"output":0.0022500000000000003,"cacheRead":0.0018078000000000002,"cacheWrite":0.000615,"total":0.0046858},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":291},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786913004927,"responseId":"msg_011Ce75VYPJeGmNeoQjWXaAZ","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_013LfnzPmPbB4rdHVMZpDkV8","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"total_markets\"\n7942\n\n(showing up to 1 rows; pass limit or aggregate to count — do not page)"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786913011588},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! So the total farmers markets (excl. territories) is 7,942.\nAnd the 2025 U.S. population is 341,784,857.\n\nNow I need to calculate: 7,942 / 341,784,857 * 100,000 = 2.3237 (to four decimal places)\n\nHowever, according to the instructions, I must use tools to do the math and never compute numbers in my head. I should create a derived metric that calculates this rate. Let me create a build script that reads both sources and joins them to calculate the metric.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll create a derived metric that calculates the farmers markets per 100,000 residents:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_015eTkEowav2NZA8wf2ZX1wx","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/build_farmers_markets_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener()\n_o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]\nu.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\n# Read farmers markets data\nfm = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"farmers_markets\",\n    storage_options=so,\n)\n\n# Read census population data\ncensus = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"census\",\n    storage_options=so,\n)\n\n# Calculate total farmers markets excluding territories\nfm_total = (\n    fm\n    .filter(fm.state_name != 'Puerto Rico')\n    .filter(fm.state_name != 'Virgin Islands')\n    .aggregate(total_markets=fm.farmers_markets.sum())\n    .mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n)\n\n# Get US population from census\nus_pop = (\n    census\n    .filter(census.NAME == 'United States')\n    .select('POPESTIMATE2025')\n    .mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n)\n\n# Join and calculate rate per 100,000\nexpr = (\n    fm_total\n    .join(us_pop, fm_total.k == us_pop.k)\n    .mutate(\n        markets_per_100k=fm_total.total_markets / us_pop.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000\n    )\n    .select('total_markets', 'POPESTIMATE2025', 'markets_per_100k')\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":12,"output":773,"cacheRead":18570,"cacheWrite":497,"totalTokens":19852,"cost":{"input":0.000012,"output":0.0038650000000000004,"cacheRead":0.0018570000000000001,"cacheWrite":0.00062125,"total":0.006355250000000001},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":138},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786913011589,"responseId":"msg_011Ce75VzdNiuAjVVnxuCMYR","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_015eTkEowav2NZA8wf2ZX1wx","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 1405 bytes to .xorq/scripts/build_farmers_markets_per_capita.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786913018527},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I'll build this script and add it to the catalog.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01BWJ3fttXiCkKewwGDL5K36","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/trial-pi-88-hmf5xulu && xorq build .xorq/scripts/build_farmers_markets_per_capita.py --builds-dir .xorq/builds --emit-build-path-to /tmp/bp_metric.txt && cat /tmp/bp_metric.txt"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":13,"output":148,"cacheRead":19067,"cacheWrite":817,"totalTokens":20045,"cost":{"input":0.000013,"output":0.0007400000000000001,"cacheRead":0.0019067,"cacheWrite":0.00102125,"total":0.00368095},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":18},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786913018527,"responseId":"msg_011Ce75WXr64E2VoHGVva